-- House Dark — 0018_trust_us_corpus
--
-- The supplied House Dark 500: the finite recommendation universe for
-- Trust Us (handover docs/handover/09_FILM_LIBRARY_500.md).
--
-- 0016 built the machinery — get_trust_us_recommendation(), the
-- exclusion set, the editorial gate — but the corpus behind it was two
-- seeded rows. A member asking the House for something tense would have
-- been told the House had nothing to offer.
--
-- Three decisions worth stating.
--
-- films.runtime_minutes was `not null`. A corpus film has no runtime
-- until an external provider enriches it, and Trust Us never shows one:
-- the recommendation is title plus six words, nothing else. Openings
-- carry their own runtime_minutes for the sealed card, so the column on
-- films was only load-bearing for the opening flow, which no longer
-- reads it. Inventing 0 or 90 to satisfy a constraint would have put
-- false data in front of the Library, so the constraint moves instead.
--
-- territories is the matching key in 0016. Each film gets its primary
-- theme plus its search tags, so free text resolves through the tags
-- into the curated theme rather than into an open catalogue.
--
-- editorial_approved_at is set on import. These 500 lines arrive
-- human-curated, exactly six words, and marked spoiler-safe in the
-- source — that is the approval 0016 is gating on. Approving them here
-- is recording a decision already made, not bypassing one.

alter table films alter column runtime_minutes drop not null;


